    {
      "id": "4814bf66-6c38-41b8-88e8-f79b511f0a56",
      "projectId": "9367e7f1-22bd-44ab-a570-bb9d55eef701",
      "title": "2025.05.15 - Prompt Management Run Through",
      "description": "Prompt Management Run-through (Retool<>Change)\nMay 15, 2025  •  43 mins  •  \nView Meeting\n or \nAsk Fathom\n\nAction Items ✨\n\nSchedule sync meetings for next week (Mon/Tue/Thu) + bi-weekly Friday demo\nLuigi Poole (he/him)\n\nProvide updated API documentation (incl. new base URL post-monolith split)\nLuigi Poole (he/him)\n\nShare early Swagger doc internally w/ Nymbl team\nGonzalo Fernandez Plaza\n\nCreate visual spec in Figma file for prompt management/testing UI\nEd Urgola\n\nAdd Change.org team (Ed, Jack, Luigi) to ClickUp project\nChase Brosseau\nMeeting Summary ✨\n\nMeeting Purpose\nReview and plan implementation of prompt management and testing features for Change.org's elections app using Retool.\nKey Takeaways\nPrompt management UI will allow editing, versioning, and testing of various prompt types (content, onboarding, recommendations)\nAPI integration will use WebSocket for real-time updates and dry-run testing without database writes\nUI work can begin immediately; API documentation and staging environment access coming soon\nWeekly syncs and ClickUp for task tracking to be set up for ongoing collaboration\nTopics\nElections App Overview\nApp helps voters understand ballot contents and make informed choices\nUses deep research documents and AI to generate summaries, race info, and personalized recommendations\nPrompts categorized into content, onboarding, and recommendation types\nPrompt Management Interface\nTable structure with groupings for different prompt types\nFields include prompt overview, settings (model, temperature, etc.), prompt text, improvements, and versioning\nConsideration for abstracting shared elements like style across prompt categories\nTesting Functionality\nData variant testing: Same prompt, different cities/candidates\nPrompt variant testing: Different prompts/settings, same data\nSide-by-side comparison crucial for efficient refinement\nPotential for bulk testing (e.g., 1000 candidates) with CSV export\nTechnical Implementation\nRetool for UI, custom API for backend processing\nWebSocket for real-time updates during prompt testing\nDry-run mode to prevent unintended database writes\nConsideration for local storage in Retool DB for work-in-progress prompts\nCollaboration and Development Process\nBreaking monolith into three services; some downtime expected next week\nAPI documentation (Swagger/YAML) to be provided for integration\nWeekly sync meetings to be scheduled (Mon, Tue, Thu; bi-weekly Friday demos)\nClickUp for task tracking, shared with Change.org team\nNext Steps\nSchedule weekly sync meetings starting next week\nProvide API documentation (Swagger/YAML) to Nymbl team\nBegin UI implementation in Retool\nSet up ClickUp for shared task tracking\nEd to create visual spec in Figma for further discussion\nNymbl team to debrief and plan initial development tasks",
      "status": "done",
      "stageId": "4a731e9d-a4f6-44fd-9524-0e9f306985ba",
